From ae7840f3f9b023e39e55d7c16bf151c50166c00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prasanth Dendukuri <prasden@amazon.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 08:02:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [CHERRYPICK FIPS 3.x] Support SSL_OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF
 option (#3294) (#3301)

### Description of changes:
CPython only exposes ssl.OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF when the linked libssl
defines this macro. Because AWS-LC
does not define it, Python 3.10+ built against AWS-LC raises
ssl.SSLEOFError: EOF occurred in violation of protocol on an unexpected
EOF whenever a peer closes the TLS connection without sending a closure
notification.

### Testing:
Added SSLTest.IgnoreUnexpectedEOF, which enables the option, closes the
server's write side without a close_notify, and asserts the client's
SSL_read returns SSL_ERROR_ZERO_RETURN.


This PR adds SSL_OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF. When enabled, an unexpected
transport EOF (the peer closing without a close_notify alert) is
reported as a clean shutdown with SSL_ERROR_ZERO_RETURN instead of
SSL_ERROR_SYSCALL

